WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:03.189
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here!

00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:07.800
As I said in my review, The Secret Life of
Pets is basically Toy Story for animals, with

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.280
Duke as Buzz Lightyear and Max as Woody, but
there are also some pretty cool references

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.510
to other movies as well as Illuminations'
own Minions and Despicable Me films.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:20.179
So, in this video, I'm going to look at some
of the best easter eggs the filmmakers snuck

00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:24.140
into the movie and if you spotted any others,
I'd love to hear about them in the comments

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.140
below.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.230
There will of course be a few spoilers ahead,
so if you want to avoid those you can click

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:33.210
or tap up in the top right of the screen for
my spoiler-free review of the movie.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:38.030
Minions is Illumination's most successful
movie to date so, as well as making the hilarious

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:42.180
short film Mower Minions, which plays before
the main movie, the studio's animators also

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:45.829
included a good number of Minions easter eggs
in The Secret Life of Pets itself.

00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:49.420
There's a Minions toy which you can see on
this boy's bedside table as well as another

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:53.719
one that's out of shot, as well as a Minions
magnet on the fridge in Katie's apartment

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:58.250
and further down the fridge there's a postcard
featuring the Minions' favourite food, a banana!

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:02.000
Plus, during the mid-credits scene the pug
Mel wears a Minions fancy dress outfit to

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.720
a party at the apartment of the head-banging
poodle Leonard.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.750
In the scene where Duke drags Max around by
the lead, the song "Happy" can be heard playing

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.280
in a taxi cab in the background.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.380
"Happy" was one of numerous songs that Pharrell
Williams composed and performed for the soundtrack

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:20.610
of Despicable Me 2 and was nominated for Best
Original Song at the Oscars.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:24.240
The name Zarelli's, which was the Italian
restaurant where Gru went on a disastrous

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.870
date in Despicable Me 2, appears on the streets
of New York though this time it's Zarelli's

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.509
Shoes.

00:01:30.509 --> 00:01:35.120
There's a poster for Illumination's next animated
feature, Sing, on the back of the bus that

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.200
Snowball drives when he chasing after the
Animal Control truck.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:43.560
Sing is a musical comedy set in a world entirely
inhabited by animals and stars Matthew McConaughey,

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:49.260
Reese Witherspoon, Seth MacFarlane and Scarlett
Johansson among many others.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:53.490
And during that scene, the way the Flushed
Pets gang swarm onto the bridge and slide

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:58.299
down cables, readying themselves to attack
Max the dog, has echoes of the scene towards

00:01:58.299 --> 00:02:04.500
the end of Rise of the Planet of the Apes
where the apes overrun Golden Gate Bridge.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.190
And the killer instincts of the crazy bunny
Snowball and the way he attacks the Animal

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:12.260
Control officer are a nice nod to the Killer
Rabbit of Caerbannog from Monty Python And

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:16.890
The Holy Grail, and his demented laughter
also reminded me of the evil bunny Boingo

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:17.890
from Hoodwinked.

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:24.330
There's a visual shout-out to Alfred Hitchcock's
classic horror film The Birds via a framed

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:30.660
poster you can glimpse, suitably enough, in
the home of the budgerigar Sweet Pea.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.740
There's a lovely little homage to the end
of director Billy Wilder's classic romantic

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:38.320
comedy Some Like It Hot when the old Basset
Hound Pops asks Chloe where she's from, and

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.600
she replies, "Dude I'm a cat", to which Pops
says: "Well, nobody's perfect".

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.310
That's actually the closing line from Some
Like It Hot, which Joe E Brown's character

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:50.630
says to Jack Lemmon after Lemmon, who's disguised
as a woman, reveals that he can't marry Brown

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:51.630
as he's actually also a man!

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:56.170
And there's a cool reference to Marilyn Monroe,
who also starred in Some It Hot, in the painting

00:02:56.170 --> 00:03:01.490
of Gidget in her apartment that's inspired
by Andy Warhol's famous "Marilyn Diptych".

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:06.460
There's an hilarious riff on the movie Grease
in the sausage factory scene where we see

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:10.470
a fantasy sequence of sausages singing and
dancing to the hit musical's closing song

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:11.700
"We Go Together".

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.760
On top of that, the choreography and geometric
shapes in the sausage song-and-dance scene

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.280
also pay homage to the musical numbers staged
by famed director and musical choreographer

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:26.810
Busby Berkeley, whose movies include 42nd
Street and Babes In Arms.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.920
Director Chris Renaud cameos in the movie
as the voice of the guinea pig Norman who

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.940
spends the movie trying to find his way back
home through the ventilation shafts in Max's

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.100
apartment block.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:38.450
Renaud's daughter Kiely also cameos as the
voice of Molly.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:43.180
And Jane The Virgin star, Jaime Camil, plays
Fernando, the star of Gidget's favourite telenovela,

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.180
La pasión de la pasión!

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.810
So guys, did you spot any other interesting
easter eggs in The Secret Life of Pets and

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.180
what did you think of the movie?

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.480
Let me know in the comments below.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:57.470
And if you enjoyed this, do like, share and
subscribe and also check out my easter egg

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:01.950
playlist or you might like to check out some
amazing deleted scenes from the animated movies

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.100
Finding Dory and Zootopia in my deleted scenes
playlist.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.800
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.200
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

